  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWith https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9841 it is possible to author a `commandfor` button inside a form, with the expectation that it will trigger the command. However based on the discussions in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9625#issuecomment-2464496320 we opted to make a `<form><button commandfor=>..` a no-op, instead encouraging users to add `type=button` to make it work. This is to prevent compatibility issues with old browsers which will end up submitting the form as they don't recogniser the `commandfor=` attribute.\n\nThis issue tracks an eventual goal of lifting this restriction, such that `<form><button commandfor=>..` works like a invoker command button, rather than a no-op. We can lift this restriction when there is sufficiently low compat risk, which we estimate may be in ~5 years time.\n\nThis relates to https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10462.",
